  "interpretation": "Optional bounded FIFO cache reuses admitted surviving HP translations in both eager enumeration and lazy expansions. Every chance trace is reused unchanged; KO-boundary predictions fall back to the engine. Both arms have a 60-second search limit, a nonbinding engine-work limit, and the same node limit. The HP-normalized input key is computed once per eager cell. Actual execution counts and cache hits are reported separately; more processed scripts or nodes alone do not prove better bounds. One run per policy and arm is a performance diagnostic, not a precise speed estimate or a policy-strength claim. The cache is disabled by default. Full-information first-decision bounds do not certify the deployed blind policy."
